  "script": "The front of the 2011 Corvette Z06 3LZ features a striking, aggressive grille design that includes a lower air intake, reflecting its high-performance nature. A distinctive Z06 badge proudly displayed on the side fender signals its high-performance pedigree, hinting at what lies beneath the hood. At the rear, prominent quad exhaust tips further emphasize the Z06\u2019s performance-oriented design, ready to unleash a thrilling roar. Under the hood lies the heart of the beast: a 7.0-liter LS7 V8 engine with striking red 'Corvette' lettering, delivering 505 horsepower and 470 lb-ft of torque. The six-speed manual gearbox embodies driver-focused engagement, enhancing the Z06 experience with its precise shift pattern. This Corvette generation was aimed at surpassing rivals like the Porsche 911. With 505 hp to the 911 Carrera S\u2019s 385 hp, the Z06 stands out in power. Its original MSRP was about $75K, but today it can be found for around $40K, marking a depreciation rate of about 7% per year. Would you choose the roaring power of the Z06 over the precision of the 911? Let us know your pick.",
